      "content": "I mean letting go of the pressure to keep existing for some imagined purpose—not because it's \"bad\" to stay, but because you're exhausted from pretending it matters. If life is truly neutral, then ending it isn't a tragedy, but it also isn't a solution—it's just a stop. The real question isn't whether it's logical, but whether you're willing to keep enduring the weight for the sake of a few moments that might not even come. You don't have to decide today, but please don't make that choice alone—talk to someone who can sit with you in the dark.",
