    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but if it's just a \"stop\" in a neutral equation, then why is there so much stigma against it? if life is just a series of random events with no objective meaning, then choosing the end is just as valid as choosing the beginning. it's just math. how can you say it's not a tragedy when the math says it's all equal?",
